export const GOAL_NOTE = "---\ntitle: My goal and interests\n---\n\n# My goal and interests\n\n## The goal\n\nBecome a cracked ML engineer with deep infrastructure knowledge and tooling (backend engineering), able to work across fields, particularly quantitative finance and blockchain. Know the systems deeply enough to read, reproduce and write research papers.\n\n## The main path\n\n**ML and AI is the spine.** Machine learning, AI research and AI systems (agents, post-training, RL for reasoning, interpretability, scaling, efficient inference, recursive self-improvement) are where I want to be top-tier. Most of my time goes here.\n\n- **Serving it:** software engineering, C++ and backend infrastructure, so I can build and run ML systems at scale. Mathematics underneath everything.\n- **Where I apply it:** blockchain, payments and banking, and quantitative finance. These are side tracks, not equal goals: they get steady time and projects, never the bulk of a week.\n- **Projects:** mostly AI projects; others where they apply ML or the systems I'm learning.\n- **Writing serves it too:** I want to write well (essays, technical posts, abstracts and papers) and share my thinking on ML and AI. Writing is thinking. Tide reviews and teaches; it never writes for me.\n\n## Interests\n\n**The spine**\n- Machine learning, ML engineering and AI research: agents, post-training, RL, interpretability, scaling, inference\n\n**Serving it**\n- Software engineering from binary upward, C++ and systems, Rust\n- Backend engineering, infrastructure and tooling; data engineering\n- Mathematics: probability and statistics, linear algebra, calculus, optimisation\n\n**Where I apply it**\n- Blockchain and blockchain engineering, stablecoins\n- Payments, payment infrastructure, core banking, open banking\n- Quantitative finance and risk, computational economics\n\n**Also**\n- Research: reading papers, reproducing results, writing my own\n- Building products (startups) and being ready for top-tier interviews\n"

